# Compact Use-Case Diagram — entity-centric

> **Reading rule.** Roles sit on the perimeter, entities in the middle.
> Each arrow is one or more verbs from a role onto an entity. When the
> verbs on a single arrow would exceed two/three, a sub-entity is split
> out (e.g. `Lesson`, `Grade`, `Request`, `Comment`).
>
> View-only interactions (browse courses, read transcript, open inbox)
> are intentionally omitted — only state changes are shown.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    %% ==========================================================
    %%  STYLES
    %% ==========================================================
    classDef stud  fill:#FDEBD0,stroke:#D35400,stroke-width:2px,color:#000
    classDef emp   fill:#D6EAF8,stroke:#2980B9,stroke-width:2px,color:#000
    classDef priv  fill:#F4ECF7,stroke:#8E44AD,stroke-width:2px,color:#000
    classDef ent   fill:#FFFFFF,stroke:#2C3E50,stroke-width:2.5px,color:#000
    classDef sub   fill:#FEF9E7,stroke:#B7950B,stroke-width:1.5px,color:#000
    classDef cap   fill:#E8F8F5,stroke:#1ABC9C,stroke-width:2px,stroke-dasharray:5 3,color:#000

    %% ==========================================================
    %%  ACTORS  (roles around the perimeter)
    %% ==========================================================
    Student((🎓 Student / Grad)):::stud
    Teacher((👨‍🏫 Teacher)):::emp
    Manager((📊 Manager)):::emp
    Librarian((📚 Librarian)):::emp
    Tech((🛠️ TechSupport)):::emp
    EmpRes((🔬 EmpResearcher)):::emp
    Dean((👔 Dean)):::priv
    Admin((🛡️ Admin)):::priv

    %% Capability — Student / Teacher / EmpResearcher opt-in
    Researcher{{🧪 Researcher}}:::cap

    %% ==========================================================
    %%  ENTITIES  (grouped by domain — labels are nouns only)
    %% ==========================================================
    subgraph ACAD [📚 Academics]
        direction TB
        Course[Course]:::ent
        Lesson[Lesson]:::sub
        Grade[Grade]:::sub
        Request[Request]:::sub
    end

    subgraph LIB [📖 Library]
        Book[Book]:::ent
    end

    subgraph COMM [💬 Communication]
        direction TB
        News[News]:::ent
        Comment[Comment]:::sub
        Message[Message]:::ent
    end

    subgraph OPS [⚙️ Operations]
        direction TB
        Order[IT Order]:::ent
        Org[Organization]:::ent
        Account[User Account]:::ent
    end

    subgraph RES [🔬 Research]
        direction TB
        Paper[Paper]:::ent
        Project[Project]:::ent
    end

    %% ==========================================================
    %%  STRUCTURAL RELATIONS  (dashed — "belongs to")
    %% ==========================================================
    Lesson  -.->|belongs to| Course
    Grade   -.->|on Course| Course
    Grade   -.->|of Student| Student
    Comment -.->|on| News
    Request -.->|may target| Course
    Paper   -.->|published in| Project

    %% ==========================================================
    %%  ACADEMICS
    %% ==========================================================
    Student -->|enroll / drop| Course
    Manager -->|create / configure / delete| Course
    Manager -->|add| Lesson
    Manager -->|assigns to course| Teacher
    Teacher -->|teaches| Course
    Teacher -->|record| Grade

    Student -->|submit| Request
    Manager -->|approve / reject| Request
    Dean    -->|approve / reject| Request

    %% ==========================================================
    %%  LIBRARY
    %% ==========================================================
    Librarian -->|add / remove| Book
    Student   -->|borrow / return| Book
    Teacher   -->|borrow / return| Book

    %% ==========================================================
    %%  COMMUNICATION  (news + comments + DMs)
    %% ==========================================================
    %% Publish News — any Employee (Manager, Teacher, Dean, Librarian, Tech, EmpRes)
    Manager & Teacher & Dean & Librarian & Tech & EmpRes -->|publish / pin| News
    Admin -->|generate top-researcher| News

    %% Comments and DMs — every authenticated role (universal)
    Student & Teacher & Manager & Dean & Librarian & Tech & EmpRes & Admin -->|write| Comment
    Student & Teacher & Manager & Dean & Librarian & Tech & EmpRes & Admin -->|send| Message

    %% ==========================================================
    %%  OPERATIONS
    %% ==========================================================
    %% Submit IT order — any Employee
    Manager & Teacher & Dean & Librarian & Tech & EmpRes -->|submit| Order
    Tech -->|accept / complete| Order

    Student -->|create / join| Org

    Admin -->|create / delete| Account

    %% ==========================================================
    %%  RESEARCH  (capability-gated)
    %% ==========================================================
    Student -.->|become researcher| Researcher
    Teacher -.->|become researcher| Researcher
    EmpRes  -.->|always| Researcher

    Researcher -->|publish| Paper
    Researcher -->|create / join| Project
    Researcher -->|subscribe / unsubscribe| Project

    %% ==========================================================
    %%  MISC
    %% ==========================================================
    Student -->|rate| Teacher
    Teacher -->|complain about| Student
```

## Why sub-entities

| Cluster that needed splitting | Without sub-entity | With sub-entity |
|---|---|---|
| Manager touches Course in 6 ways | `Manager --create/configure/delete/add-lesson/set-prereq/set-capacity/assign-teacher--> Course` (unreadable) | `Manager --create/configure/delete--> Course` + `Manager --add--> Lesson -.belongs-to.-> Course` |
| Teacher records grades; Student sees them | `Teacher --record-marks-for-Student-in-Course--> ???` (3-way relation) | `Teacher --record--> Grade -.on.-> Course` + `Grade -.of.-> Student` |
| Student↔Manager have request flow tied to Course | `Student --submit-request-about-Course--> Manager` (4-way) | `Student --submit--> Request -.may-target.-> Course` + `Manager --approve/reject--> Request` |
| News supports comments | `Student --comment-on-News--> News` (verb hidden in noise) | `Student --write--> Comment -.on.-> News` |

## How to read it

- **Solid arrow** = an action a role performs on an entity (state change).
- **Dashed arrow** = a structural relationship (sub-entity → parent, capability → role).
- **Hexagonal node** (`Researcher`) = capability, opt-in for Student/Teacher and always-on for EmpResearcher.
- **Light-yellow boxes** = sub-entities introduced solely to keep arrow labels short.

## Role groupings used in the diagram

These multi-source arrows (written with Mermaid's `&` syntax) match the
actual API gating:

| Group | Members | Used for |
|---|---|---|
| Any authenticated role | Student, Teacher, Manager, Dean, Librarian, Tech, EmpRes, Admin | `write Comment`, `send Message` |
| Any employee | Manager, Teacher, Dean, Librarian, Tech, EmpRes | `publish News`, `submit Order` |
| Request approvers | Manager, Dean | `approve / reject Request` |
| Book borrowers | Student, Teacher | `borrow / return Book` (only these two roles hold `BookBorrowerCapable`) |
